title: Windsor Chair
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Named in England in the 1720s. Chairs built the same way are older than that.

A solid wood seat with the legs and the back spindles socketed straight into it. All wood.

No one designer. A way of building that many makers shared and changed.

See [[Shaker Ladder Back]], [[Vernacular]].

